## Overview

This is an OfficeFloor-based fork of Spring PetClinic. Creating an owner is `POST /owners`, defined as a chained pipeline in a YAML file where each step names a Java function class. The owner-creation functions live under `.../rest/function/owner/`.

## 1. Registration date — set / defaulted

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DefaultRegistrationDate.java`
```java
14  public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
15      if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
16          owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
17      }
18  }
```
- Supplied date path: the request date arrives via the DTO. `registrationDate` is a field of `OwnerFieldsDto` (declared in `openapi.yml:2046-2051`, "Defaults to the server's current date when omitted"). It flows into the domain object in `BuildOwner.java:11-13` (`built.set(ownerMapper.toOwner(request))`), so a supplied value is already on the `Owner` and `DefaultRegistrationDate` leaves it untouched.
- Defaulted path: when omitted, `DefaultRegistrationDate` sets it to `LocalDate.now()` (raw server date, no adjustment).
- The field/column: `Owner.java:55-56` (`registration_date`), getter/setter at `102-108`.

## 2. Membership number generation (year segment)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`
```java
50  default String membershipNumber(Owner owner) {
51      if (owner == null || owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
52          return null;
53      }
54      return String.format("%s-M%02d", owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
55  }
```
- Format: `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` = last two digits of the **registration date's** year (`getYear() % 100`), e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`. Wired as a derived DTO field at `OwnerMapper.java:25`.
- The `customerCode` part is produced separately by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java` (`AssignCustomerCode.java:16-22`): format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, a per-city 4-digit sequence.
- Spec: `openapi.yml:2111-2118` documents `membershipNumber` (example `SMI-0007-M26`).
- Note the ordering dependency: in the POST pipeline `defaultRegistrationDate` runs (line 41-44) before `assignCustomerCode` (46-49), and the membership number is only computed later at DTO-mapping time, so both `customerCode` and `registrationDate` are populated by then. The "year segment" is driven entirely by whatever `registrationDate` ended up being (supplied or defaulted).

## 3. Daily create-limit (owners per day)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureDailyOwnerLimit.java`
```java
16  static final int DAILY_LIMIT = 100;
18  public void service(OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DailyOwnerLimitException {
19      LocalDate today = LocalDate.now();
20      long registeredToday = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
21              .filter(owner -> today.equals(owner.getRegistrationDate()))
22              .count();
23      if (registeredToday >= DAILY_LIMIT) {
24          throw new DailyOwnerLimitException(DAILY_LIMIT);
25      }
26  }
```
- Counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; at 100+ it throws.
- Escalation type: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyOwnerLimitException.java` (carries the limit).
- Handler → HTTP 429: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler.java:10-13` (`HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`).
- Escalation wiring: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DailyOwnerLimitException.yml` maps the exception to the handler class.

Ordering caveat worth flagging: `ensureDailyOwnerLimit` runs early in the pipeline (before `build`/`defaultRegistrationDate`), and it counts by `today = LocalDate.now()`. So the limit is enforced against owners dated today regardless of what date the current request supplies.

## 4. OfficeFloor REST YAML + function classes for POST /owners

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` — the full create pipeline. Relevant steps in order:
- `ensureCityCapacity` → `ensureDailyOwnerLimit` (lines 24-30) — the create-limit check.
- `build` → `defaultRegistrationDate` → `assignCustomerCode` → `assignHousehold` → `countNamesakes` → `save` → `respond` (lines 36-68), all under `govern: [ transaction ]`.
- Authorization guard at top: `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` (line 2).

Each `class:` entry maps to a file in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/` (e.g. `BuildOwner.java`, `DefaultRegistrationDate.java`, `AssignCustomerCode.java`, `SaveOwner.java`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`). Other owner endpoints: `owners.GET.yml` and the `owners/` subdirectory in the same api folder.

## 5. Existing tests

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
```java
15  void coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay() throws Exception {
16      int id = createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
17      DayOfWeek dow = LocalDate.parse(fetchOwner(id).get("registrationDate").asText()).getDayOfWeek();
18      assertTrue(dow != DayOfWeek.SATURDAY && dow != DayOfWeek.SUNDAY, dow.toString());
19  }
```
- This asserts the **default** `registrationDate` is never a weekend (a "business-day roll forward to Monday" invariant, per the comment at lines 9-11).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — the harness/helpers:
- `createMany(int n)` (lines 181-187): creates n owners dated today — the driver for "per-day create-limit / bulk-signup rules".
- `fillCity` (170-179), `fetchOwner` (199-204), `extractId` (206-219).
- Business-day helpers: `HOLIDAYS` set (239-242) and `toBusinessDay(LocalDate)` (267-274) which rolls over weekends **and** the pinned holidays.
- Class-level comment (line 37) lists the derived features under test: "membership number, per-day cap, per-city cap, most common city".

## Notable inconsistency to be aware of

The acceptance test `coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` and the `AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay`/`HOLIDAYS` machinery expect the **defaulted** registration date to be rolled forward to the next business day (skipping weekends and holidays). But `DefaultRegistrationDate.java:16` simply assigns `LocalDate.now()` with no weekend/holiday adjustment. So the implementation does not currently perform the business-day roll that the tests describe — the test only passes on days that already happen to be business days. If a business-day default is intended, the logic in `DefaultRegistrationDate` is the place it would live (and would in turn shift the membership-number year segment and the daily-limit comparison, since both key off `registrationDate`/`LocalDate.now()`).

